## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | lib/src/cli/agent_cli_compaction.dart | ⚠️ important the busy phase try finally guard was dropped from both relief call sites the old code cleared the compacting context… busy label in a finally dart pushbusyphase compacting context… try await runautocompact auto compacted finally pushbusyphase the new code clears it only on the success path dart pushbusyphase compacting context… final reliefoutcome await runemergencyrelief pushbusyphase emergencyrelief run s own failure safety covers only appendhiddenrange emergency relief dart 319 329 its re anchor and view build i o — refreshagentstate → session buildcontextmessages line 186 and session getbranch session getentries in buildview lines 336 341 — sit outside that guard and can still throw torn corrupt session jsonl i o failure on such a throw the label is never cleared the loop s catch agent loop dart 1624 turns the relief into no relief and the turn ends on the terminal guard error — printed under a stuck compacting context… busy row that is exactly the reads as a dead stall face the removed finally was introduced to prevent issue 1085 m3 comment right above this line the window is bounded the row drops when the run settles but the regression is on the exact lines this pr rewrote and costs one line to restore please wrap the relief await in try finally in both sites relieveoverwindow and relievemessagecap same shape at line 1002 1004 |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | lib/src/compaction/emergency_relief.dart | 💡 suggestion vetoed docstring claims an exempt user veto the code does not implement the doc says the veto covers three things dart the shared safety veto the protected tail a pinned expansion or an exempt real user record in the group — all or none bool vetoed set string protectedtail set string pinnedrecordids but the body checks only protectedtail and pinnedrecordids — there is no exempt real user check unlike the quality tier s validatehidepicks which drops exempt picks explicitly structured judge dart 100 105 entry exempt today the behavior is safe only structurally pair groups are built from an assistant carrier its toolresultmessage s structured ledger dart 313 343 pairgroups so a user record can never ride inside a tool group and the new unit test pins the observable outcome but the doc on a freshly exported public engine class asserts a safety check that does not exist — the next change to group formation or a reader porting this veto elsewhere inherits a guarantee the code never provided either narrow the doc tool pair groups structurally never contain exempt user records — see pairgroups or add the explicit exempt check for defense in depth mirroring validatehidepicks |
| F3 | open | SUGGESTION | lib/src/compaction/emergency_relief.dart | 💡 suggestion speculative public api — run int targettokens and ledgercache have no callers both knobs ship on the newly exported emergencyrelief class but nothing in production or tests uses them run int targettokens — every caller cli runemergencyrelief the flutter relieveoverwindow all 12 unit tests relies on the default window settings reservetokens this ledgercache final ledgerentrycache ledgercache — the doc says scope it to one session like every other cache owner but no owner scopes one the relief is a once per overflow event not a hot loop this repo s own doctrine for the append only barrel is explicit lib flutter agent harness dart 143 147 gh 1232 api stays internal until a caller exists — a speculative export is the wrong order emergencyrelief itself absolutely belongs in the barrel it has two production callers the suggestion is to drop the two speculative parameters until a consumer exists — they are trivial to re add but a public class in the package barrel is contract surface every future change must preserve |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

